---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="FE Simulation of Shock Waves in Energetic Materials — Alejandro Riaño-Molina"
  description="Finite element analysis of localized high-temperature-rate regions in energetic materials under shock wave loading. Research conducted at Purdue University."
  lang="en"
>
  <nav id="navbar">
    <a href="/" class="nav-logo">ARM<span>.</span></a>
    <ul class="nav-links">
      <li><a href="/#projects">Projects</a></li>
      <li><a href="/#contact">Contact</a></li>
      <li><a href="/es/projects/energetic-materials" class="lang-toggle"><span class="current">EN</span> / ES</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <main class="project-page">
    <a href="/#projects" class="project-back"><span>←</span><span>Back to projects</span></a>

    <div class="section-tag">Project 02 · 2023–2024 · Purdue University</div>
    <h1>FE Simulation of Shock Waves in Energetic Materials</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="opacity:1; animation:none; max-width:720px; margin-top:1rem;">
      Finite element analysis of localized high-temperature-rate ("hotspot") regions in energetic materials under shock wave loading.
    </p>

    <div class="project-meta">
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Institution</span><span class="value">Purdue University</span></div>
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Advisor</span><span class="value">Dr. Marisol Koslowski</span></div>
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Role</span><span class="value">Undergraduate Research Assistant</span></div>
      <div class="project-meta-item"><span class="label">Tools</span><span class="value">ANSYS · FEA · Python post-processing</span></div>
    </div>

    <!--
      MAIN IMAGE / VIDEO:
      Place a hero image at /public/images/projects/energetic-hero.jpg
      (1600×900 — e.g. temperature contour plot on the shocked geometry, or
      a snapshot of the mesh with the shock front).
      Recommended VIDEO option: /public/videos/energetic-loop.mp4 — a short
      muted loop showing the temperature evolution. This is the kind of asset
      that catches a recruiter's eye in 2 seconds.
    -->
    <div class="project-hero-media placeholder" data-label="Place a shock-wave temperature field render here · /images/projects/energetic-hero.jpg or /videos/energetic-loop.mp4">
      <img src="/images/projects/energetic-hero.jpg" alt="Shock wave simulation" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
    </div>

    <div class="project-section">
      <h3>Context</h3>
      <p>
        When a shock wave propagates through an energetic material, the response is not homogeneous: a small
        fraction of the volume concentrates a disproportionate amount of energy in regions known as <em>hotspots</em>.
        These localized high-temperature-rate zones are the precursors to initiation, and understanding their formation
        is central to both safety analysis and detonator design.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-section">
      <h3>Approach</h3>
      <p>
        Using <strong>ANSYS</strong>, I set up coupled thermo-mechanical finite element simulations of representative
        microstructures subjected to shock loading. The work focused on:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Identifying the geometric features (pores, voids, interfaces) that drive hotspot formation.</li>
        <li>Quantifying the temperature rise rate as a function of shock pressure and microstructural geometry.</li>
        <li>Post-processing fields in Python to extract statistical descriptors of the hotspot distribution.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="project-gallery">
      <div class="project-hero-media placeholder" data-label="/images/projects/energetic-mesh.jpg">
        <img src="/images/projects/energetic-mesh.jpg" alt="FE mesh" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
      </div>
      <div class="project-hero-media placeholder" data-label="/images/projects/energetic-temp.jpg · Temperature field">
        <img src="/images/projects/energetic-temp.jpg" alt="Temperature field" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="project-section">
      <h3>Outcome</h3>
      <p>
        The simulations contributed to an ongoing line of research in Dr. Koslowski's group on multiscale modeling
        of shock-induced initiation. The experience was, more broadly, my first formal exposure to U.S. research
        culture and a direct path into my current Ph.D. work at Michigan.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-next">
      <a href="/projects/hydrogen-embrittlement">← Previous: Hydrogen Embrittlement</a>
      <a href="/projects/nasa-herc-rover">Next: NASA HERC Rover →</a>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <span class="footer-text">Alejandro Riaño-Molina <span>·</span> Ann Arbor, MI</span>
    <span class="footer-text">Built with Astro <span>·</span> Hosted on GitHub Pages</span>
  </footer>

  <script is:inline>
    const navbar = document.getElementById('navbar');
    window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
      navbar.classList.toggle('scrolled', window.scrollY > 40);
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
